  <h2>Two outerwear families, one freight bill</h2>

  <h3>Technical shells &amp; gorpcore (Arc'teryx, TNF, CP Company)</h3>
  <p>
    Hard-shell and soft-shell rows emphasise tape seams, zipper stacks, and hood articulation.
    <strong>Arc'teryx</strong> and <strong>The North Face</strong> appear in both parka and jacket pools—shoppers often confuse similar thumbnails.
    QC focus: logo emboss alignment, seam taping continuity, cuff velcro symmetry.
    These pieces are lighter than down puffers but still bulky—read <a href="/blog/spreadsheet-volumetric-chargeable-weight-basics/">chargeable weight basics</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Down &amp; fur-trim parkas (Canada Goose, Moncler, Moose Knuckles)</h3>
  <p>
    Down lanes are freight-heavyweights.
    <strong>Canada Goose</strong>, <strong>Moncler</strong>, and <strong>Moose Knuckles</strong> recur in parka rows; badge and arm patch QC is non-negotiable.
    A single puffer can bill like multiple hoodies once the warehouse measures DIM weight—<a href="/blog/winter-puffer-jacket-shipping-volumetric-hacks/">puffer volumetric hacks</a> are essential before you promise friends a landed total.
  </p>

  <h3>Streetwear &amp; logo outer (Trapstar, Supreme, Balenciaga)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Trapstar</strong> and <strong>Supreme</strong> puffers trade on graphic placement; <strong>Balenciaga</strong> appears in both shell and oversized silhouette rows.
    Print alignment and zipper pull branding matter more than on basics—use <a href="/blog/kakobuy-4k-qc-video-inspection-guide/">4K QC video</a> when stills hide curvature defects.
  </p>

  <h3>Luxury &amp; heritage (Burberry, Fendi, Louis Vuitton)</h3>
  <p>
    Trench and logo-forward rows cluster under <strong>Burberry</strong>, <strong>Fendi</strong>, and <strong>Louis Vuitton</strong> strings.
    Plaid symmetry and button spacing are classic retake triggers.
    Branded leather trim can push outbound routes into stricter lanes—<a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded vs. unbranded shipping</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Stone Island &amp; badge culture</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Stone Island</strong> shows in both jacket and parka snapshots.
    Compass badge stitching, button dye, and arm patch position separate acceptable batches from instant RL items.
    Pair picks with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">apparel sizing notes</a>—Italian sizing drift hurts more on structured shoulders.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for outerwear rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Badge / arm patch:</strong> compass points, embroidery density, attachment angle.</li>
    <li><strong>Zipper &amp; hardware:</strong> branded pulls, tape colour match, snag tests in video QC.</li>
    <li><strong>Down fill &amp; quilting:</strong> even baffles, no obvious clumping in warehouse lighting.</li>
    <li><strong>Fur trim (if applicable):</strong> verify colour and attachment—common bait-and-switch vector.</li>
    <li><strong>Interior labels &amp; wash tags:</strong> size confirmation before you approve export.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Community QC archives help research batches—<a href="/blog/community-crowdsourced-qc-verification-batches/">crowdsourced verification</a>—but warehouse photos remain authoritative.
  </p>

  <h2>Freight &amp; packaging tactics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Rehearsal packaging:</strong> measure before you commit to a line—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-rehearsal-packaging-freight/">rehearsal guide</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Vacuum/compress when offered:</strong> down recovers after airing; freight savings may be worth it.</li>
    <li><strong>Split branded vs. unbranded outbound:</strong> mixing a Moncler puffer with unbranded tees can complicate route eligibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Seasonal timing:</strong> buy parkas off-peak when possible—<a href="/blog/annual-reps-shopping-calendar-2026/">2026 reps calendar</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Budget framing</h2>
  <p>
    Outerwear item prices span wide ¥ bands, but freight often dominates landed cost for single-piece carts.
    Model scenarios in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-first-haul-budget-planner-2026/">first haul budget planner</a> before you treat a ¥400 parka as “cheap shipping because one item.”
  </p>

  <h2>Browse workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Start at <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/jackets/">Jackets</a>.</li>
    <li>Decide shell vs. down early—they ship differently.</li>
    <li>Copy live listing URLs; avoid screenshot pastes (<a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">link hygiene</a>).</li>
    <li>Approve QC on badges and quilting, not seller studio lighting.</li>
    <li>Quote freight on measured dims; consider rehearsal if near a bracket edge.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Outerwear rewards patient buyers.
    The spreadsheet gets you to a credible row; Kakobuy measurements and your QC discipline determine whether the coat that arrives is worth the cubic centimetres it consumed.
  </p>
